Hacking on quickstep
===================

Coding style
------------

ISO C99, enforced with -std=c99 -pedantic.  Do not use C11 features
(_Static_assert, <stdatomic.h>, _Alignas, anonymous unions, _Generic);
if one is wanted, wrap it in a macro with a C99 fallback.  Follow the GNU Coding
Standards: GNU indentation, a space before the opening parenthesis of
calls and declarations, return type on its own line in definitions, and
no tabs beyond what GNU indent produces.  Every public symbol starts with
gq_ (types and functions) or GQ_ (macros, enumerators).  The library
exports nothing else.

Every source file carries the GPLv3+ notice used in the existing files.

Push-parsing contract (required for every codec)
------------------------------------------------

  * Input arrives in chunks.  The parser never blocks and never reads
    from a file descriptor.
  * Parsers take (const uint8_t **buf, size_t *len), consume what they
    can, and advance both.  Whatever is left is an incomplete unit that
    the caller keeps and presents again with more data appended.
    GQ_NEED_MORE reports that case; it is not an error.
  * One forward pass.  No seeking back, no split-then-parse pipeline.
  * Output is a stream of semantic events to a handler.  Variable-length
    payloads are slices into the caller's buffer.  Do not allocate an
    object graph for parsed content and do not buffer whole messages.
  * State machines are explicit (an enum plus small scratch fields), not
    hidden in the call stack.
  * Unit tests must feed the same input whole and in every chunk size
    from 1 upwards and compare the resulting event logs.  See
    tests/test-frame.c.

Cryptography
------------

Never implement a primitive.  Everything comes from libgcrypt through
src/crypto.c, or from the trust backend through src/trust.c.  New
algorithms need a known-answer test from the defining RFC or NIST
document.

Warnings
--------

The tree must build with zero compiler warnings (configure adds -Wall
-Wextra and more).  Fix the cause; if a warning is genuinely
unavoidable, add a narrow, commented suppression.  Read the build
output, not just the exit status.

Testing
-------

  make check              # unit tests
  make check-integration  # integration tests
  make distcheck          # before every release

make check runs unit tests only (tests/): deterministic, in-process, with
no sockets, files, child processes or wall clock (the engines take their
clock as a hook, and the loopback tests run on a virtual one), and fast
enough to run on every change.  Anything that needs real I/O, another
program, the host's own files or trust store, or the real clock goes in the
integration suite (integration/), which make check-integration builds and
runs and make check never touches:

  interop.sh          TLS against OpenSSL and GnuTLS (interop-client and
                      interop-server are our side); needs openssl and
                      optionally gnutls-serv and gnutls-cli
  interop-dtls.sh,
  interop-dtls12.sh   DTLS 1.3 and 1.2 against wolfSSL, OpenSSL and GnuTLS
  interop-quic.sh     QUIC against quiche (QUICHE_DIR names its programs)
  quic-interop-runner/smoke.sh
                      the quic-interop-runner endpoint against itself
  integ-files         key loading from a file, the system trust store

Each skips itself (exit 77) when what it needs is missing.  Set
GQ_NO_INTEROP=1 to skip the interop scripts, or OPENSSL / GNUTLS_SERV to
choose the binaries.

ML-DSA needs a GnuTLS built with leancrypto (./configure --with-leancrypto);
the distributions' GnuTLS does not have it, so the ML-DSA unit tests (in
test-sign, test-trust, test-tls-server and test-conn) note that they are
skipped.  A skipped test must not look like a passing one where the backend
is meant to be there: with GQ_EXPECT_MLDSA=1 in the environment they fail
instead.  CI runs them that way in the "ML-DSA" job, built by the
check-mldsa target of integration/quic-interop-runner/Dockerfile:

  docker build --target check-mldsa -f integration/quic-interop-runner/Dockerfile .

Copyright assignment
--------------------

The project intends to become part of the GNU system with copyright
assigned to the Free Software Foundation.  Until then, keep the notice
"Copyright (C) YEAR Name" in each file, and do not incorporate code
whose licence is not compatible with GPLv3+.

Documentation and translation

The manual is Texinfo (doc/quickstep.texi); update it with any change to
design, policy or roadmap.  Build it with "make info" or "make pdf".

Every string a person might read (for example the text returned by
gq_strerror) must be wrapped in _() from src/gettext.h and its source file
listed in po/POTFILES.in.  Do not translate RFC-defined identifiers.
Check that the configure step reports "checking whether to use NLS: yes";
on systems where libintl is not in the default path pass CPPFLAGS and
LDFLAGS for it.
